Had to square the elements of array and then sort them for O(n) complexity.
Make the result array to store the elements.
make left point to start and right point to end of the array.
and position at last too cause we will fill the element from the end as we know the biggest element would be  at starting or end 
because the input array is sorted.
Now, we check if (abs(nums[left])>abs(nums[right]) if it is then we square the nums[left] and store it at the end of result array
Now increase left and dec position because we want to check for next value.
else if value from right is greater than left we square right value and add to result dec position and right.

code---
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> sortedSquares(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int> result(nums.size()) ;
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.size()-1;
        int position = nums.size()-1;
        while(left<=right){
            if(abs(nums[left])>abs(nums[right])){
                result[position] = nums[left]*nums[left];
                left++;
            }else{
                result[position] = nums[right]*nums[right];
                right--;
            }
            position--;
        }
        return result;
    }
};
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)
Extra auxiliary space excluding the output array: O(1)
